    <summary type="text">I use Universal Blue&#39;s Aurora distribution on my daily driver desktop, and I rebooted today which led what I imagine is a kernel update. This broke all of my...</summary>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;I use Universal Blue&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href=&#34;https://getaurora.dev/en&#34;&gt;Aurora&lt;/a&gt; distribution on my daily driver desktop, and&#xA;I rebooted today which led what I imagine is a kernel update. This broke all of&#xA;my &lt;a href=&#34;/docker/&#34; class=&#34;glossary-term&#34; title=&#34;docker - container runtime&#34; data-hover-title=&#34;docker&#34;&gt;docker&lt;/a&gt; containers using a GPU.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvidia-container-cli: detection error: open failed: /usr/lib/libnvidia-tls.so.570.153.02: no such file or directory: unknown&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thankfully a reboot and booting into the older environment fixes everything&amp;hellip;&#xA;Linux and immutability FTW&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;related&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;Related&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#related&#34; class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://universal-blue.discourse.group/t/cannot-use-nvidia-runtime-in-docker-since-update-to-fedora-42/8812/3&#34;&gt;Discorse Thread&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;</content>
